text:
The day Is dull, and dark, and dreary,
There's smoke, and the chimney's never weary;
The blur elings to the same old gall,
But from every stack the CRIME must fall,
And the day is dark and dreary.
Ones life Is dull, and dark and dreary;
OF CRIME and dirt ones ever weary;
Ones thoughts still cling to a cleaner past.
But the hopes OF youth get the smoky blast,
And the days are dark and dreary.
Be still. sad heart! and cease repining;
Behind the smoke the suns still shining;
Thy fate Ia the common fate of all,
Into each life much SCOT must fall,
And days be dark and dreary.


Indianapolis News.

